{
  "note": "Expected values (SPEC2 §9.5), verified read-only on medziokle-prod on 2026-10-09. exact = closed season; floor = running season (≥); exactOn = exact when snapshotDate equals date, else floor. A re-snapshot that moves a closed-season value updates this file in the same commit and adds a line to \"changes\".",
  "changes": [
    "2026-10-09: first snapshot. Damages small-cell rule (owner decision): every damages count of 1 or 2 is published as '<3'. National per-group livestock totals (cls \"*\") are published, computed on unsuppressed data.",
    "2026-10-09: privacy.mjs added (no new query). '<3' now also covers 0 for every sibling cell of a published row, so small counts cannot be worked out from the totals; escalated counts are published only for kanopiniai and bebrai; municipalities with fewer than 3 MPV (Klaipėdos m., Neringos) are pooled in loots and limits. Damages month rows: 49 -> 90 (complete grid); national escalated '*' no longer published.",
    "2026-10-09: privacy.mjs also protects derived figures (no new query): the remainder of a sum over several '<3' or withheld cells, and reports minus escalated, may not be 1 or 2. 27 more damages cells withheld (shown as 'neskelbiama'), among them Lietuva stumbrai 2025, vilkai ozkos 2026 (9 animals) and lusys avys 2026 (5 animals)."
  ],
